/*
MDC Rule: Gutenberg Block Best Practices

- Use functional React components and hooks for all block logic.
- Use `@wordpress/i18n` for all strings (never hardcode user-facing text).
- Use `useBlockProps` for block root elements.
- Use BEM or CSS modules for class naming.
- Avoid direct DOM manipulation; use React state and effects.
- Use prop-types or TypeScript for type safety.
- Use async/await for data fetching; show loading states.
- Write unit tests for all components and hooks.
- Document props, hooks, and utilities with JSDoc or TypeScript.
- Keep all block logic modular and reusable.
*/
